target:
NARRATIVE: To check if two lines are parallel, we need to compare their slopes. Two lines are parallel if their slopes are equal. The slope of a line in 3D space can be derived from the coefficients of the line equation Ax + By + C = 0, which is the same as the direction vector (A, B). If the direction vectors of the two lines are proportional, then the lines are parallel.

For the given lines, we can extract the direction vectors from the coefficients. If the ratios of the corresponding components of the direction vectors are equal, then the lines are parallel.

ACTION: {"expression":"all([line1[i] / line2[i] == line1[0] / line2[0] for i in range(1, 3)])"}

